2. Detection models — downloaded, not committed
------------------------------------------------
`scripts/export_models.py` downloads two third-party checkpoints at setup time. Neither is
included in this repository and neither is covered by its licence.

  PPE / helmet / vest    melihuzunoglu/ppe-detection            YOLOv11  — AGPL-3.0
  Fire / smoke           SalahALHaismawi/yolov26-fire-detection YOLOv26  — MIT

The PPE detector is a YOLOv11 model and the export path uses Ultralytics, both AGPL-3.0. This is
why this repository is AGPL-3.0 as well. If you replace the detectors with models under different
terms, the obligations that follow from those models are yours to determine.


3. Tracker configuration — `configs/tracker_nvsort_tuned.yml`
--------------------------------------------------------------
A modified copy of NVIDIA's NvSORT tracker configuration, retaining its original
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 header. Copyright (c) NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES.

Three values differ from the stock config (minTrackerConfidence, probationAge,
minIouDiff4NewTarget); the reason is documented in project_skill.md §6, trap 14.


4. Runtime dependencies — not redistributed here
-------------------------------------------------
NVIDIA DeepStream SDK, TensorRT, CUDA and JetPack are installed separately and are subject to
NVIDIA's own licence agreements. mediamtx (MIT) and llama.cpp (MIT) are downloaded at setup time.
Python dependencies are listed in `requirements/` and retain their own licences.


